  "content": {
    "id": "p3-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Two students, Annie and Bianca, each choose a number between $1$ and $5$ inclusive. By listing all the possible outcomes, find the probability that:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p3-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "they both choose an even number",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{4}{25}$",
          "worked": "Write outcomes as (Annie's number, Bianca's number). The complete list is\n$$\\begin{gathered}(1,1),(1,2),(1,3),(1,4),(1,5),\\\\(2,1),(2,2),(2,3),(2,4),(2,5),\\\\(3,1),(3,2),(3,3),(3,4),(3,5),\\\\(4,1),(4,2),(4,3),(4,4),(4,5),\\\\(5,1),(5,2),(5,3),(5,4),(5,5).\\end{gathered}$$\nThere are $25$ equally likely outcomes. Both numbers are even in $(2,2),(2,4),(4,2),(4,4)$.\n$$P(\\text{both even})=\\frac{4}{25}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 19
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Bianca chooses a larger number than Annie",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{2}{5}$",
          "worked": "The favourable outcomes are $(1,2),(1,3),(1,4),(1,5),(2,3),(2,4),(2,5),(3,4),(3,5),(4,5)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{Bianca larger})&=\\frac{10}{25}\\\\P(\\text{Bianca larger})&=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the product of their numbers is greater than $10$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{8}{25}$",
          "worked": "The favourable outcomes are $(3,4),(3,5),(4,3),(4,4),(4,5),(5,3),(5,4),(5,5)$. Products equal to $10$ are excluded.\n$$P(\\text{product}>10)=\\frac{8}{25}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "the sum of their numbers is less than $6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{2}{5}$",
          "worked": "The favourable outcomes are $(1,1),(1,2),(1,3),(1,4),(2,1),(2,2),(2,3),(3,1),(3,2),(4,1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{sum}<6)&=\\frac{10}{25}\\\\P(\\text{sum}<6)&=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
